    "name": "ofi_concord_wide_gate",
    "mechanism": "Stress-UNLOCKED flow conviction, one-sided claim: cross-window same-sign OFI is scored only when the quoted spread is unusually WIDE vs its trailing 300s, and set to exactly zero outside that regime. The hypothesis is narrower than the product form's: conviction under stressed quoting is informed queue investment (makers fearful, yet one-sided limit flow persists across both windows -> deliberate positioning) and continues at 15-60s, while conviction under normal or tight quotes makes NO directional claim at all -- it is switched off rather than claimed to revert. Economically this isolates the rare informed-positioning episodes from the mass of routine flow; the nonzero support is a strict subset of the product's, so its cross-sectional structure (mass of exact zeros plus stressed-only signals) differs from both the bare base and ofi_concord_x_spread_z. Dedup note: within the wide regime the value is monotone in the base, so rank correlation vs the base is diluted only by the zero mass -- expect moderate, not negligible, sibling corr with the product.",
